{
  "notes": {
    "* header/senderISName@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. The workbook gives chars=an, so the generated XSD keeps a system's name to Latin letters, digits, hyphen and space; today's shared header had no class. A Cyrillic name would be refused: a question for the spec team (HEL-26).",
    "* header/messageId@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today's type restricts messageId to the uuid pattern [a-zA-Z0-9\\-]+; the workbook gives min=36, max=36 alone, so the generated XSD is looser.",
    "* header/messageType@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today's shared pattern ([RPCIXH][0-9]{3}) leaves out D and L, so today's XSDs refuse every e-Dental messageType; the generated XSD fixes the value and applies the workbook's an class.",
    "* contents/dentalTreatment/lrn@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today's lrn has the an class; this workbook gives max=36 alone.",
    "* contents/lrn@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today's lrn has the an class; this workbook gives max=36 alone.",
    "* contents/results/dentalTreatment/lrn@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today's lrn has the an class; this workbook gives max=36 alone.",
    "* contents/dentalTreatment/basedOn@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. The workbook makes basedOn an NRN, min=12, max=12, chars=an; today's type allowed any 36 characters.",
    "* contents/results/dentalTreatment/basedOn@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. The workbook makes basedOn an NRN, min=12, max=12, chars=an; today's type allowed any 36 characters.",
    "* contents/subject/email@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today's email type has the pattern [^@]+@[^.]+\\..+; the workbook gives max=255 alone.",
    "* contents/results/subject/email@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today's email type has the pattern [^@]+@[^.]+\\..+; the workbook gives max=255 alone.",
    "* contents/performer/email@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today's email type has the pattern [^@]+@[^.]+\\..+; the workbook gives max=255 alone.",
    "* contents/results/performer/email@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today's email type has the pattern [^@]+@[^.]+\\..+; the workbook gives max=255 alone.",
    "* contents/performer order unexplained": "Real drift, and a wire difference (HEL-26). Today's medicalPractitioner extends medicalPractitionerSimple, so its own fields follow the base's: pmi qualification practiceNumber phone email, then pmiDeputy role rhifAreaNumber nhifNumber. The workbook interleaves them. A message in today's order is refused by the generated XSD; the spec team settles which order NHIS reads.",
    "* contents/results/performer order unexplained": "Real drift, and a wire difference (HEL-26). Today's medicalPractitioner extends medicalPractitionerSimple, so its own fields follow the base's: pmi qualification practiceNumber phone email, then pmiDeputy role rhifAreaNumber nhifNumber. The workbook interleaves them. A message in today's order is refused by the generated XSD; the spec team settles which order NHIS reads.",
    "* contents/performer/pmi@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today exactly 10 digits; the workbook max=10, chars=n (e-Referral is not consistent either, HEL-24).",
    "* contents/performer/pmiDeputy@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today exactly 10 digits; the workbook max=10, chars=n (e-Referral is not consistent either, HEL-24).",
    "* contents/results/performer/pmi@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today exactly 10 digits; the workbook max=10, chars=n (e-Referral is not consistent either, HEL-24).",
    "* contents/results/performer/pmiDeputy@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today exactly 10 digits; the workbook max=10, chars=n (e-Referral is not consistent either, HEL-24).",
    "* contents/results cardinality unexplained": "Real drift. Today at most 20 results; the workbook 0..*.",
    "* contents/results/dentalTreatment/dentalProcedure/status cardinality unexplained": "Real drift. The workbook requires the procedure's status; today it is optional.",
    "* contents/error/description cardinality unexplained": "Real drift. The shared error type allows one description; the workbook any number.",
    "* contents/error/description@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. The shared error description holds 2000 characters; the workbook min=1, max=255.",
    "* header/senderISName only-published unexplained": "Real drift. Today's shared header requires senderISName in every message, responses included; the workbook lists it in requests only. NHIS sends the responses, so a vendor only reads them, but a response without it is refused by today's XSD."
  },
